        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-30 04:05:50.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20565 tests: use EC_* layouts in sanity-ec extend tests",
        "message": "LU-20565 tests: use EC_* layouts in sanity-ec extend tests\n\nsanity-ec subtests 8a-8c and 8e-8l (lfs mirror extend --ec) hard-coded\nan EC 4+2 layout on 4-stripe data mirrors with a gate of 6 OSTs,\nalthough each tests a mirror extend rule, not the geometry.  They\nwould be skipped on the 4 OST test sessions.\n\nUse the EC_ARG, EC_DSTRIPE and EC_CSTRIPE defaults that enable_ec()\nscales to OSTCOUNT, and EC_DSTRIPE data stripes, so they run with 3\nOSTs.  Put each PFL boundary in front of an EC component on a\nmultiple of the row width.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-ec\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-ec ostcount=4\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I48317fe17e7e538210970c657ffc55ba2f3ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
